  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sudan Acute Crisis Joint Response (SDN ACJR)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">World Relief (WR) and HOPE will provide integrated Health and Protection support to address the urgent needs of 18,766 people. The response will focus on 3 localities in Um Algura, Sharg Aj Jazirah, Al Hasahisa in Al Jazira State. The interventions are needed due to inflow of IDPs and overwhelming pressure on current facilities. The interventions will complement the WASH/FSL interventions from ZOA in Um Algura and Sharg Aj Jazirah. 

4 existing health-centers will be supported to continue providing services, by distributing essential and life saving drugs and medical equipment.  

2 mobile clinics will be deployed in more remote locations to provide PHC in line with the Health sector guidelines. 

HOPE will provide PSS to address wellbeing of 1,500 children. Awareness raising sessions on GBV will be provided to ensure the rights and safety of children and women.  1200 girls and women at risk will receive protection kits in line with protection cluster guidelines.</narrative>
  </description>
